e Winterlake mansion, now a hospital, when twin girls go missing, only to wake up in a bathtub wired to old medical equipment. From there, this survival horror game has her explore the derelict building, solve puzzles, manage resources and fight off the horrors between her and the truth.\n\nThe design follows the fixed-camera tradition of Alone in the Dark and the early Resident Evil games, with a dynamic camera and updated controls to smooth out the format. Expect slow, deliberate pacing and tense encounters. Single-player, with full controller support, and aimed at fans of classic survival horror who want that style with modern polish."}}